{"id":"baja-1000-2025","title":"SCORE Baja 1000 (2025)","who":"SCORE International · 58th edition","when":"November 2025","vehicle":"Off-road race: trucks, buggies, motorcycles, quads","kind":"rally","color":"#dc2626","summary":"The world's most famous off-road race, on Mexico's Baja California peninsula since 1967. The 2025 race was an 854-mile counter-clockwise loop from Ensenada south past San Quintín to San Ignacio and back up the Gulf side through San Felipe. The 2026 race starts and finishes in Los Cabos, and the classic Ensenada–La Paz run returns for the 60th anniversary in 2027.","sources":[{"label":"131 Offroad: 2025 Baja 1000 course","url":"https://131offroad.com/2025/10/04/2025-baja-1000-course"},{"label":"SCORE Journal, October 2025","url":"https://read.uberflip.com/i/1540550-score-journal-oct-2025/25"},{"label":"RACER: Menzies and Polvoorde win the 2025 Baja 1000","url":"https://racer.com/2025/11/16/menzies-polvoorde-storm-to-score-baja-1000-redemption"}],"approximate":"Main points and race-mile checkpoints; the course runs on desert tracks, not the roads shown.","km":1528,"bbox":[-116.6025,27.2836,-112.8946,31.902],"stops":[{"name":"Ensenada","place":"Ensenada, Baja California","at":[31.8659,-116.603],"text":"Start and finish, in the city that has hosted the race for decades."},{"name":"San Quintín (RM 212)","place":"San Quintín, Baja California","at":[30.5614,-115.9381],"text":"First physical checkpoint near race mile 212.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Pescar_en_la_bahia_de_San_Quintin_MX.jpg/500px-Pescar_en_la_bahia_de_San_Quintin_MX.jpg","page":"San Quintín, Baja California","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pescar_en_la_bahia_de_San_Quintin_MX.jpg","credit":"Ll1324","license":"CC0"}},{"name":"San Ignacio (RM 365)","place":"San Ignacio, Baja California Sur","at":[27.2837,-112.8979],"text":"An oasis town of date palms; the southern turn of the loop at race mile 365.","photo":{"url":"https: